    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31856" root="غسل" body-key="g">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غِسْلَةٌ</span></b> : see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غَسُولٌ</span>: ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  and see also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غِسْلٌ</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3- 
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَلَى وَجْهِهِ غِسْلَةٌ</span> means <i>His face is beautiful,
with no fat,</i> or <i>fatness, upon it.</i> (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b4-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَبُو</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غِسْلَةَ</span> is an appellation of <i>The wolf:</i> (O, K:) and
so <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ابو عِسْلَةَ</span>, with <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ع</span>. (TA.)

  </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
